::GEO_U02_UA_Q01::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_UA_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.1<br><br>Question:<br>Which rule translates a point 3 units left and 2 units up? {
= (x, y) &rarr; (x - 3, y + 2)#Correct. (x, y) &rarr; (x - 3, y + 2) matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ (x, y) &rarr; (x + 3, y - 2)#This choice reflects a misconception: (x, y) &rarr; (x + 3, y - 2). Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ (x, y) &rarr; (-x, y)#This choice reflects a misconception: (x, y) &rarr; (-x, y). Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ (x, y) &rarr; (y, x)#This choice reflects a misconception: (x, y) &rarr; (y, x). Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

